BW__learnContent"><header><h1>Introduction to Bit Manipulation</h1></header=
><h2 id=3D"intuition">Intuition</h2>
<p>Bit manipulation is a technique used in programming to perform operation=
s at the bit level, which can often lead to more efficient and faster algor=
ithms.</p>
<p><strong>When is bit manipulation useful?</strong><br>
<!-- -->Bit manipulation allows us to work directly with the binary represe=
ntation of numbers, making certain operations more efficient. Common tasks =
such as setting, clearing, toggling, and checking bits can be performed qui=
ckly using bitwise operators.</p>
<p>For example, one of the most common space optimization techniques involv=
es using an unsigned 32-bit integer to represent a set of boolean values, w=
here each bit in the integer corresponds to a different boolean value. This=
 allows us to store and manipulate up to 32 states without using a boolean =
array or hash set.</p>
