<p>Some useful characteristics of the XOR operator are:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>a ^ 0 =3D a</code></li>
<li><code>a ^ a =3D 0</code></li>
</ul>
<p>In addition, it=E2=80=99s also important to understand the fundamental s=
hift operators:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Left shift (<code>&lt;&lt; n</code>)</strong>: Shifts the bits o=
f a number to the left by <code>n</code> positions, adding 0s on the right.=
 This is equivalent to multiplying a number by <code>2n</code>.</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><=
img alt=3D"Image represents a visual example of a left bit shift operation.=
