hift of two positions. The bottom row displays the result of the operation:=
 '1 0 0 1 0 0', also within a peach-colored rectangle.  Four orange arrows =
connect the top row's digits to their corresponding shifted positions in th=
e bottom row, visually demonstrating how each bit is moved two places to th=
e left.  The '=3D', symbol to the left of the bottom row signifies that it =
represents the outcome of the bit shift operation on the input sequence." l=
oading=3D"lazy" width=3D"342" height=3D"90" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=3D=
"1" style=3D"color:transparent" src=3D"https://bytebytego.com/images/course=
